    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30181" root="علث" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُلْثَةٌ</span></b> , with damm, (K, but written in the O
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلْثَة</span>,) <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُلْقَةٌ</span> [most probably, I think, in the
sense in which this is used in the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِى فِى</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا المَالِ عُلْقَةٌ</span> (q. v.), from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَعَلَّثَ</span> in the first of
the senses assigned to it above, syn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَعَلَّقِ</span>].
(O, K.)

